<AtTheTable>

Update with both blockers and public actions. Label action likelihoods as assumptions unless you have enough representative observations to estimate them.

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>

Bayesian updating combines a prior belief with the likelihood of new evidence. A precise posterior can still be misleading when the likelihood model is poorly chosen.

</QuantCorner>
